# Review: IbkrPlugin

The core is built and well covered by unit tests. The connector maps token and query id; the Flex client
paces, polls past retryable codes and stops on rate-limit codes; the sync and import operations append
`PortfolioReport`s to the feed the read operations parse; `MaterializeInstrument` is idempotent and
folds new keys; `GetInstrumentFundamentals` reads SEC EDGAR through the CORS proxy; and the daily
trigger is parented to the Portfolio. The gaps are mostly at the edges. There is no
`PortfolioSyncAction` component (sync is an inline toolbar action in `PortfolioArticle`, and connect comes
from `ConnectorAuthAnnotation`). Flex and SEC errors are untyped `Error`s or a single `IbkrSyncError`, so
callers cannot tell RateLimited from FetchFailed. `FundamentalsValuation` is never filled, and the SEC
client does no pacing. Containers import parsers and `resolveTradingViewSymbol` from the `services` barrel,
which also exports the HTTP clients. None of the assistant behaviour (F-4.2 to F-4.5, T-10) is tested. The
code also adds a persisted `Lot` type and a `SyncLots` operation that the spec does not describe.

Of 72 items: 35 done, 19 untested, 15 partial, 1 diverged, 2 missing.

## Extensions

